[2026-03-14T21:36:01.224Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q1TSdCA9Ghy81kUbb927fW","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# LinearClone — Project Management App\n     2→\n     3→A project management application inspired by Linear, designed for software development teams to track issues, plan sprints, and manage projects with a clean, fast, keyboard-friendly interface.\n     4→\n     5→## Core Concepts\n     6→\n     7→- **Workspace**: The top-level container. Each workspace has its own projects, teams, and members. For this app, there is a single workspace.\n     8→- **Team**: A group of members working together (e.g., \"Engineering\", \"Design\"). Each team has its own set of issues, cycles, and views.\n     9→- **Project**: A cross-team initiative that groups related issues toward a larger goal. Projects have a status, target date, lead, and progress bar based on completed issues.\n    10→- **Issue**: The fundamental unit of work. Issues have a title, description, status, priority, assignee, labels, project, and cycle.\n    11→- **Cycle**: A time-boxed iteration (like a sprint). Each team can have one active cycle at a time.\n    12→- **Label**: Tags for categorizing issues (e.g., \"Bug\", \"Feature\", \"Improvement\").\n    13→- **Member**: A user in the workspace who can be assigned issues and belong to teams.\n    14→\n    15→## Authentication\n    16→\n    17→Simple email-based authentication (no OAuth). Users sign up with name, email, and password. On first login, a default workspace is created. Sessions are managed via a session token stored in localStorage.\n    18→\n    19→### Pages\n    20→\n    21→- **Login Page** (`/login`): Email + password fields, \"Sign in\" button, link to sign up.\n    22→- **Sign Up Page** (`/signup`): Name, email, password fields, \"Create account\" button, link to login.\n    23→\n    24→## Navigation\n    25→\n    26→A collapsible left sidebar present on all authenticated pages:\n    27→\n    28→### Sidebar Sections\n    29→\n    30→1. **Workspace Header** — Workspace name at top, clickable to go to home.\n    31→2. **Main Navigation**:\n    32→   - My Issues (icon: user-circle)\n    33→   - Inbox (icon: inbox) — Shows notification count badge\n    34→3. **Team Section** — For each team:\n    35→   - Team name as section header (collapsible)\n    36→   - Issues (icon: list)\n    37→   - Active Cycle (icon: refresh-cw)\n    38→   - Projects (icon: folder)\n    39→   - Views (icon: layout) — Saved filtered views\n    40→4. **Workspace Section**:\n    41→   - All Projects (icon: folder)\n    42→   - All Teams (icon: users)\n    43→   - Members (icon: user-plus)\n    44→   - Labels (icon: tag)\n    45→   - Settings (icon: settings)\n    46→\n    47→The sidebar should be collapsible to icon-only mode via a toggle button.\n    48→\n    49→## Issue Statuses\n    50→\n    51→Issues flow through these statuses (each with a distinct icon and color):\n    52→\n    53→| Status       | Icon         | Color   |\n    54→|-------------|-------------|---------|\n    55→| Backlog      | dotted circle | gray    |\n    56→| Todo         | circle       | gray    |\n    57→| In Progress  | half circle  | yellow  |\n    58→| In Review    | three-quarter circle | blue |\n    59→| Done         | check circle | green   |\n    60→| Cancelled    | x-circle     | red     |\n    61→\n    62→## Issue Priorities\n    63→\n    64→| Priority | Icon            | Color  |\n    65→|----------|----------------|--------|\n    66→| Urgent   | alert-triangle  | red    |\n    67→| High     | arrow-up        | orange |\n    68→| Medium   | minus           | yellow |\n    69→| Low      | arrow-down      | blue   |\n    70→| No Priority | dots-horizontal | gray |\n    71→\n    72→## Pages\n    73→\n    74→### My Issues Page (`/my-issues`)\n    75→\n    76→A filtered view showing all issues assigned to the current user, grouped by status. Each group is collapsible.\n    77→\n    78→**Issue Row** displays:\n    79→- Priority icon\n    80→- Issue identifier (e.g., `ENG-42`)\n    81→- Title (clickable, navigates to issue detail)\n    82→- Status icon (clickable to change status)\n    83→- Labels as small colored badges\n    84→- Assignee avatar\n    85→- Due date (if set)\n    86→- Project name (if assigned)\n    87→\n    88→**Filters toolbar** at top:\n    89→- Status filter (multi-select dropdown)\n    90→- Priority filter (multi-select dropdown)\n    91→- Label filter (multi-select dropdown)\n    92→\n    93→### Inbox Page (`/inbox`)\n    94→\n    95→Shows notifications for the current user:\n    96→- Issue assigned to you\n    97→- Issue you're subscribed to was updated\n    98→- You were mentioned in a comment\n    99→\n   100→Each notification row shows: icon for type, issue identifier, brief description, relative timestamp.\n   101→Notifications can be marked as read (click) or archived. Unread notifications are visually distinct (bold, left border accent).\n   102→\n   103→### Team Issues Page (`/team/:teamId/issues`)\n   104→\n   105→The primary issue list for a team. Similar layout to My Issues but shows all team issues.\n   106→\n   107→**Features**:\n   108→- Group by: Status (default), Priority, Assignee, Project, Label, None\n   109→- Sort by: Priority, Created date, Updated date, Status\n   110→- Filter by: Status, Priority, Assignee, Label, Project, Cycle\n   111→- Bulk actions: Select multiple issues via checkboxes, then change status/priority/assignee/label\n   112→- \"New Issue\" button opens a create issue modal\n   113→\n   114→**Issue Row** (same as My Issues but also shows):\n   115→- Checkbox for bulk selection\n   116→- Team identifier prefix (e.g., `ENG-42`)\n   117→\n   118→### Issue Detail Page (`/issue/:issueId`)\n   119→\n   120→Full issue view with inline editing for all fields.\n   121→\n   122→**Left Panel** (main content, ~70% width):\n   123→- Issue identifier and title (inline editable, large font)\n   124→- Status selector (inline dropdown)\n   125→- Description (rich text area, supports markdown, inline editable)\n   126→- **Activity / Comments section** at bottom:\n   127→  - Tab toggle: \"Activity\" | \"Comments\"\n   128→  - Activity tab shows chronological history of all changes (status changes, assignee changes, etc.)\n   129→  - Comments tab shows user comments with avatar, name, timestamp\n   130→  - Comment input box with \"Comment\" button at bottom\n   131→  - Each comment shows author avatar, name, relative timestamp, and content\n   132→\n   133→**Right Panel** (sidebar, ~30% width):\n   134→- **Status**: Dropdown selector showing current status with icon\n   135→- **Priority**: Dropdown selector showing current priority with icon\n   136→- **Assignee**: Searchable member selector with avatar\n   137→- **Labels**: Multi-select label picker with colored dots\n   138→- **Project**: Searchable project selector\n   139→- **Cycle**: Dropdown showing available cycles for the team\n   140→- **Due Date**: Date picker\n   141→- **Created**: Timestamp (read-only)\n   142→- **Updated**: Timestamp (read-only)\n   143→\n   144→**Sub-issues section** (below description):\n   145→- List of child issues\n   146→- \"Add sub-issue\" button\n   147→\n   148→### Create Issue Modal\n   149→\n   150→Triggered from any issues list page via \"New Issue\" button or keyboard shortcut."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VZCcEgJMeh3Ga6cQedHgo4","session_id":"dd761dfc-3c41-4aea-8240-b38c3f09e95a","uuid":"fc608e29-2d92-48c9-9e78-e7de09698c0f"}
