[2026-03-14T21:42:34.239Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Xicam6pHsFesvgvLmbkPDy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me verify there are no issues with the `initialCount` approach in the create test - the `count()` call is before the action, so it's fine. Let me also verify the `create-issue-modal` modal closing behavior. The modal closes after 1500ms delay. The `toHaveCount(0, { timeout: 30000 })` should handle that.\n\nNow let me also check if the `team-issue-group-items-*` testids match between the component and my tests. The component uses `team-issue-group-items-${group.key}` and `group.key` for status groups is the status name (e.g., `backlog`, `todo`, `in_progress`). This matches my tests.\n\nLet me also check that the `issue-row-` prefix selector won't accidentally match the group-level elements. The group testids start with `team-issue-group-` and the row testids start with `issue-row-`. The selector `[data-testid^=\"issue-row-\"]` should only match rows, not groups. Good.\n\nLet me verify the `create-issue-modal` disappearing. The modal overlay has `data-testid=\"create-issue-modal-overlay\"` and the modal itself has `data-testid=\"create-issue-modal\"`. When `createIssueModalOpen` is false, the component returns null, so both are removed. My test checks `create-issue-modal` which should correctly detect the removal.\n\nOne more thing - let me check: the `Newly created issue appears in the list` test gets the initial count via `await initialRows.count()` which is a snapshot. Since issues are loaded at this point (we waited for `team-issues-list` to be visible), this should be accurate. After creating the issue, the modal triggers `fetchTeamIssues(formData.teamId)` which refetches the team issues. Then the modal closes after 1500ms. The list should update with the new issue.\n\nHowever, there's a potential timing issue - the `count()` call is instant and might fire before all issue